# Jachai News

**Ground News for Bangladesh** — installable PWA that clusters the same story across Prothom Alo, Daily Star, bdnews24, BBC Bangla, and more. Compare framing, perspective lean, blindspots, rumor flags, and **verify claims** with AI-assisted fact-checking. UI copy is **English + Bangla** where product-facing.

## Repo layout

| Path | Stack |
|------|--------|
| `backend/` | Python 3.11+, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy (async), PostgreSQL (`asyncpg`, **pgvector** + FTS for claims), optional **Redis** + **Celery** (`ingest`, `verification` queues), RSS via `app/services/rss_parser.py`, ingestion in `app/services/rss_ingestion.py`, AI via `app/services/ai_client.py` (Groq default, Gemini optional) |
| `frontend/` | Next.js 15 App Router, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind, PWA (`@ducanh2912/next-pwa`); optional Supabase auth — barrel `src/lib/supabase.ts` re-exports `supabase/client.ts`, `server.ts`, `service.ts`, `config.ts`; session refresh in `supabase/middleware.ts` |
| `supabase/` | Migrations for profiles, Pro subscriptions, bKash tables, user dossiers/alerts (RLS); see `.cursor/rules/supabase.mdc` |
| Root `package.json` | `dev:frontend`, `dev:backend`, `build:frontend`, `lint:frontend`, **`ingest:backend`**, **`worker:backend`**, **`worker:verification`**, **`stack:up`** / **`stack:down`** |
| `docker-compose.yml` | Local stack: Postgres (pgvector), Redis, API, Celery worker |

## Data on the frontend

- **Live API**: `api-base.ts` — browser `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` (default `/api/v1` via Next rewrite); server `API_URL` → `http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1`. `api.ts` / `verifications.ts` use `resolveApiBase()`. News: `/articles`, `/clusters`, `/clusters/{slug}`, `/bias`, `/rumors`. GETs time out quickly via `api-resilience.ts` (`fetchJsonSafe`).
- **Verification**: `frontend/src/lib/verifications.ts` → `POST /verify`, `/verifications`, `/verifications/jobs/{id}`, SSE `/events`, WebSocket `/ws`, `/verifications/{slug}`, `/verifications/search`; progress helper `verification-progress.ts`. Reads degrade safely; submit still requires a live API.
- **Demo fallback**: Rich story payloads in `demo-data.ts` (`DEMO_STORIES`, `BD_SOURCES`, `DEMO_RUMOR_ARTICLES`); `stories.ts` merges API clusters with demo by slug and falls back when the API is down or empty. UI signals offline/demo with `ApiDegradedBanner` (`fromApi` flags).
- **Home feed**: `/` is static shell + `HomeStoryGridClient` — paints demo stories first, then hydrates from **`GET /api/feed/top`** (`app/api/feed/top/route.ts` → `getTopStories`, short public cache).
- **Resilience**: `app/error.tsx` + `global-error.tsx`; `ClientErrorBoundary` on heavy client widgets (`StoryTabs`, `VerifyClaimForm`). Prefer extending `stories.ts` / `api.ts` / `verifications.ts` rather than fetching ad hoc in pages.

## RSS ingestion (backend)

- **Service**: `backend/app/services/rss_ingestion.py` — seed sources from `bd_sources_seed.py`, fetch feeds, dedupe by article URL, cluster by title Jaccard similarity (72h lookback, threshold ~0.42), optional AI cluster summary via `ai_client.summarize_cluster` when 2+ articles in a cluster.
- **CLI**: `npm run ingest:backend` → `backend/scripts/ingest_rss.py` (requires `DATABASE_URL`; ORM tables + SQL migrations on API startup).
- **API**: `POST /api/v1/ingest` in `app/api/ingest.py`; optional `INGEST_API_KEY` env → require `X-Ingest-Key` header; async via Celery when `REDIS_URL` + `INGEST_ASYNC_ENABLED`.
- **Ops hooks**: `app/services/ops_alerts.py` — Healthchecks.io start/success/fail pings and optional Telegram summaries on ingest; wired from `ingest.py` and `scripts/ingest_rss.py`. All no-ops when env vars are unset.

## Claim verification (backend + UI)

- **Submit (product)**: `POST /api/v1/verify` (`app/api/verify.py`) — sanitize text/URL, `ai_guardrails`, semantic cache hit → instant result; else queue job (`verification_jobs` + Celery `verification` queue or `BackgroundTasks`).
- **API surface**: `app/api/verifications.py` — create/list/search/get by slug, job status, **SSE** (`/jobs/{id}/events`) and **WebSocket** (`/jobs/{id}/ws`) for progress.
- **Pipeline**: `verification_submit`, `verification_runner`, `verification_pipeline`, `semantic_cache`, `embeddings`; SQL extras in `backend/migrations/001_verified_claims_pgvector_fts.sql` via `db_extensions.apply_sql_migrations`.
- **Frontend**: `/verify` (`VerifyClaimForm`), `/verify/[slug]`, `/verify/database` (`ClaimSearch`); nav link in `SiteHeader`.

## Admin ops (internal)

- **Backend**: `GET /api/v1/admin/overview` — counts, per-source stats (incl. **`disabled`**), recent clusters (`admin_stats.py`). `POST/DELETE /api/v1/admin/sources` — add or soft-disable RSS sources (`admin_sources.py`: DELETE sets `disabled` for seed feeds or sources with articles; empty custom rows are deleted; POST with same name re-enables). When `ADMIN_API_KEY` is set, require header `X-Admin-Key`.
- **Frontend**: production admin UI on **`admin.jachai.news`** (`admin-host.ts`; main site redirects `/admin`); local dev at `/admin`. Page gate via legacy cookie (`ADMIN_PASSWORD` + `admin-auth.ts`) **or** Supabase user with `app_metadata.role=admin` / `ADMIN_EMAILS` allowlist. Public: `/admin/login`, `/admin/register` (`ADMIN_REGISTRATION_CODE`). Server proxies: `app/api/admin/login`, `logout`, `ingest`, `register`, `verify`, **`overview`**, `sources` — backend calls through `lib/admin-api.ts` with `ADMIN_API_KEY` / `INGEST_API_KEY`. **`app/api/admin/*` mutating/read proxies** (overview, sources, ingest) require legacy **`jachai_admin`** cookie (`admin-route-auth.ts` / `verifyAdminSession`); Supabase-only admins can open `/admin` but still need legacy login for those routes until extended. UI: **`AdminDashboardPanel`** (stats + `AdminSourcesPanel`), `AdminIngestPanel`, `AdminLogoutButton`.
- **Env**: document in `backend/.env.example` and `frontend/.env.example`; never expose admin secrets as `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.

## Monitoring (optional)

- **Backend**: `app/core/sentry_init.py` (`init_sentry()` in `main.py` before app creation); `SENTRY_DSN` + related settings in `app/core/config.py`
- **Frontend**: `@sentry/nextjs` — `instrumentation.ts`, `instrumentation-client.ts`, `sentry.server.config.ts` / `sentry.edge.config.ts`; `withSentryConfig` in `next.config.ts`; `NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_*` in `frontend/.env.example`
- **Secrets**: Never commit DSNs, Telegram tokens, or Healthchecks URLs; document new vars in `backend/.env.example` / `frontend/.env.example`

## Supabase (auth + Pro — planned checkout)

- **Schema**: `20250301000000_init_profiles_subscriptions.sql` — `profiles`, `subscriptions`, `bkash_agreements`, `payment_transactions`; `20250302000000_security_rls_hardening.sql` — `saved_dossiers`, `custom_alerts`, explicit deny policies on billing writes.
- **Types**: `frontend/src/lib/database.types.ts` (keep in sync with migrations; regenerate with Supabase CLI when schema changes).
- **News + verified claims** stay in backend PostgreSQL; subscription/payment and user research metadata in Supabase.

## Product vocabulary

- **Headline clash / cluster** — Same story, different framings (cluster or story detail view)
- **Perspective** — `independent` \| `neutral` \| `establishment` \| `opposition` \| `international` (`frontend/src/lib/perspectives.ts`)
- **Bias meter** — Source or cluster lean score
- **Rumor badge** — Low corroboration or speculative coverage (`is_rumor` on articles)
- **Blindspot** — Story marked one-sided (`isBlindspot` on demo `Story` type)
- **Verified claim** — User-submitted claim with AI verdict + analysis (`verified_claims`, `/verify/[slug]`)
- **Jachai Pro** — Paid tier; pricing in `frontend/src/lib/subscription-plans.ts` (৳49/mo, ৳399/yr). **Feature matrix** (free vs Pro): `frontend/src/lib/subscription-features.ts` — source of truth for gating copy and `PRO_ONLY_FEATURE_IDS`. **Entitlements**: `subscription-entitlement.ts` (`isActiveProSubscription` on `subscriptions` row); `subscription-access.ts` — `getProAccessState()` / `hasProAccess()` via Supabase RLS (server session) with `NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_PRO=true` override for local UI. Planned payment: bKash Tokenized Checkout API; no live checkout yet.

## Quality bar

- Match existing naming and file layout; minimal diffs; no drive-by refactors
- Type hints on Python public functions; strict TypeScript on frontend
- Never commit secrets; backend env via `backend/app/core/config.py` and `backend/.env.example`; frontend via `frontend/.env.local` (API URL, optional Supabase keys, optional `NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_PRO`)
